course: dictionary
lesson: 9732
title: Sunless: the word that means no sun
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Sunless» is built from two parts: sun and -less. The -less ending means without, so sunless means without sunlight. A sunless day is dark or dull, and a sunless place is one where the sun never reaches.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The shivering, sunless days!» Shivering tells you the days are cold, and cold, grey days often have no bright sunshine. So sunless fits with cold and dull.
explain: Now try the swap test. The swallow's story says «the long sunless nights and the cold» nearly finished her. Could you replace sunless with dark and still make sense? Yes, so dark is a good partner word, but sunless is more exact: it tells you the sun is missing.
fact: The ending -less means without, so sunless means without sun.
fact: «Sunless» means without sunlight; dark or dull.
fact: «Sunless» can also mean a place where the sun never reaches, like a deep cave.
fact: In science, the deep ocean is sunless, so no plants can grow there.
fact: Context clues such as «shivering» and «cold» can help you guess the meaning of an unknown word.
exercise: «The shivering, sunless days!» What does sunless mean here? | *Without sunlight, dark or dull | Warm and busy | Very windy and wild | Full of bright sunshine
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to sunless? | Sunny | Noisy | *Dark
exercise: In the swallow's story, what did «the long sunless nights and the cold» nearly do? | *Nearly finished her | Made her sing a happy song | Helped her fly south quickly | Gave her a new nest
test: A sunless place is one where... | A field of daisies in May | The top of a sunny beach | *The deep, dark sea where the sun never reaches
test: In «a sunless forest feels gloomy», which word tells you what sunless is like? | *Gloomy | Loud | Sunny | Bright
exam: The swallow flew south to the hot sun, away from the «sunless nights» of winter. What does sunless mean? | Full of birds | Cold like ice | Full of sunshine | *Without sunlight, dark and dull
